Verify that creating a measuring parameter with TEXT type accepts and stores free-form text input without injection risks,Measuring Parameter Management - Parameter Creation,Security,High,User is logged in as a shop owner with permission to create measuring parameters. The application supports TEXT type parameters for custom measurements.,"1. Navigate to the 'Add Measuring Parameter' screen in the shop management dashboard. 2. Enter a parameter name (e.g., 'Custom Note'). 3. Select 'TEXT' as the parameter type. 4. Enter a suggestive value containing special characters, script tags, and SQL-like syntax (e.g., '<script>alert(1)</script>', ""'; DROP TABLE users; --""). 5. Submit the form to create the parameter. 6. Navigate to the 'View Measuring Parameters' screen and locate the newly created parameter. 7. Verify the suggestive value is displayed exactly as entered.

Test Data: Parameter Name: Custom Note, Suggestive Value: <script>alert(1)</script> ""; DROP TABLE users; --",The measuring parameter is created successfully. The suggestive value is stored and displayed as plain text (not executed as script or interpreted as SQL). No errors or injection behavior occurs.,TC-018
Verify that creating a measuring parameter with TEXT type enforces input length limits to prevent oversized payloads,Measuring Parameter Management - Parameter Creation,Security,Medium,User is logged in as a shop owner with permission to create measuring parameters. The application supports TEXT type parameters for custom measurements.,"1. Navigate to the 'Add Measuring Parameter' screen in the shop management dashboard. 2. Enter a parameter name (e.g., 'Custom Note'). 3. Select 'TEXT' as the parameter type. 4. Enter a suggestive value with an extremely long string (e.g., 10,000 characters). 5. Submit the form to create the parameter.

Test Data: Parameter Name: Custom Note, Suggestive Value: [A 10,000-character string]","The application either truncates the input to a reasonable length (e.g., 255 characters) or rejects the request with an error message (e.g., 'Suggestive value is too long'). The parameter is not created if the input exceeds limits.",TC-019
Verify that creating a measuring parameter with TEXT type rejects null bytes or control characters in input,Measuring Parameter Management - Parameter Creation,Security,Medium,User is logged in as a shop owner with permission to create measuring parameters. The application supports TEXT type parameters for custom measurements.,"1. Navigate to the 'Add Measuring Parameter' screen in the shop management dashboard. 2. Enter a parameter name (e.g., 'Custom Note'). 3. Select 'TEXT' as the parameter type. 4. Enter a suggestive value containing null bytes or control characters (e.g., 'test␀value'). 5. Submit the form to create the parameter.

Test Data: Parameter Name: Custom Note, Suggestive Value: test␀value","The application rejects the request with an error message (e.g., 'Invalid characters in suggestive value'). The parameter is not created.",TC-020
